{"actor":"model","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-220058","model_call":24,"attempt":1,"model":"gpt-5.5","usage":{"input_tokens":13390,"output_tokens":459,"total_tokens":13849,"cached_tokens":12544,"reasoning_tokens":258},"output_characters":922,"decision":{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_03_1112857541#6_1889600581","relevance":0,"reason":"This result is about causes and medical consequences of premature birth, mentioning maternal substance abuse and trauma as causes. It does not address prematurity as a risk factor for later child abuse.","learned":"A query combining prematurity, maltreatment, and special health care needs can drift to general premature-birth causes rather than abuse-risk mechanisms."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ \"premature babies\" \"premature infants\" \"high-risk infants\") (+ \"more demanding\" \"demanding requirements\" \"higher toll\") (+ abuse \"physical punishment\" frustration))","reason":"Target the strongest known explanatory wording while broadening exact phrases to find additional non-duplicate sources explaining that premature/high-risk infants increase caregiver burden and frustration leading to abuse."}}}
