{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-220058","model_call":45,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q775"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q775"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_22_1591365968#9_3378520235","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q775","rank":2,"snippet":"with child abuse include: lack of knowledge about child development lack of knowledge about how to care for children insufficient money/income to support the needs of a child substance abuse psychological problems unbalanced family relationships domestic violence single parenting. The risk of child abuse is increased if a child's parents are young and immature, with unrealistic expectations. Parents who are young and immature may lack knowledge about child development and how to take care of children, as well as the cost of raising a child, leading to unrealistic expectations. These parents may become frustrated when their expectations aren't met. Families with children who are <cover>premature, chronically ill, or who have attention-deficit hyperactivity disorder or a mental health disorder are also at a higher risk for child abuse. </cover>These children will have more care requirements, potentially leading to burnout and increasing the risk of abuse.\" , \"start_char\": 4712.000000 , \"title\": \"The red flags of child abuse : Nursing made Incredibly Easy\" , \"url\": \"https://journals.lww.com/nursingmadeincrediblyeasy/Fulltext/2018/03000/The_red_flags_of_child_abuse.8.aspx\" }","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_49_126583413#2_254044156","rank":1,"relevance":1}]},"time":9},"model_calls":45,"document_judgments":38,"relevance_3":4,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
